  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RBM for MEPA-Save the Nature Georgia - RBM support to MEPA-Save the Nature Georgia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">RBM support to MEPA-Save the Nature Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sida st&#xf6;der Georgiens ministerium f&#xf6;r milj&#xf6;skydd och jordbruk (MEPA), som &#xe4;r genomf&#xf6;randepartner till programmet Save the Nature Georgia. St&#xf6;det omfattar perioden december 2021 till december 2024 och har en total budget p&#xe5; 58 000 000 SEK. Programmet har utvecklats i n&#xe4;ra dialog med Sida och bygger p&#xe5; den georgiska regeringens strategier och handlingsplaner f&#xf6;r biologisk m&#xe5;ngfald, luftf&#xf6;roreningar och milj&#xf6;. Som ett villkor f&#xf6;r finansiering av programmets andra fas ska MEPA under inledningsfasen utveckla programmets interventionslogik, f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsteori och resultatbaserade ramverk. F&#xf6;r detta &#xe4;ndam&#xe5;l har ambassaden beslutat att tillhandah&#xe5;lla expertst&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sidas ramavtal f&#xf6;r RBM.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sida supports the Georgia Ministry of Environment Protection and Agriculture (MEPA), implementing partner of the programme Save the Nature Georgia. The support covers the period December 2021 to December 2024 and a total budget of 58 000 000 SEK. The programme has been developed in close dialogue with Sida and based on the Georgian government&#x2019;s strategies and action plans for biodiversity, air pollution and environment. As a condition for funding the second phase of the programme, MEPA shall, during the inception phase, develop the programme&#x2019;s intervention logic, theory of change and results-based framework. For this purpose, the Embassy has decided to provide expert support from Sida&#x2019;s framework agreement for RBM.</narrative>
  </description>
